Lorraine -
<p>I hope you are doing well and that you have escaped all of the sickness going around. It&#39;s hard to believe that we met back in the fall, and now it&#39;s time for your&nbsp;blood drive!<br />
<br />
I know Kim&nbsp;has kept in close contact with you, but I just wanted to reach out to wish you well tomorrow.&nbsp; Even if your appointment schedule is full, please keep encouraging people to come to your drive. Winter is a critical time for blood donations, and we are currently experiencing many drives that are unable to reach their goal due to sickness. I know you can do it!&nbsp;<br />
<br />
If there is any help you need from me - questions, last minute ideas for recruiting, instructions on how to use our online scheduling, Stories of Hope, anything at all, please reach out. I am here to help you reach your goal to save lives. Here is a link to a recipient video you can send out to your team to remind them of why we give:</p>

<p><br />
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3_KWUxff_cg<br />
<br />
<br />
Thank you again for your commitment to saving lives through blood donation!<br />
Kirsten</p>
